[metadata]
- in_text_citation: [(Hunyadi et al., 2017-08)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/0b3e3428a2e9a28098d9a9aa2597ff0905fe61b7)
- venue: Journal of Neuroscience Methods
- citation count: 42
[method]
The paper quantified zebrafish larval seizures from non-invasive local field potential (LFP) recordings rather than calcium imaging. Manual analysts marked epileptiform events in 10-minute recordings, and an automated system extracted time- and frequency-domain features, used NLEO and length thresholds (tau_NLEO and tau_len), and trained multiple classifiers separately for a chemical PTZ/VHC model and a genetic model. Classifier selection used leave-one-recording-out cross-validation on training data and chose the best model by cross-validated positive predictive value. The method evaluated seizure frequency per 10-minute recording, cumulative seizure duration, number of seizing larvae (at least three seizures), and, for expected-seizure groups, sensitivity, specificity, positive predictive value, accuracy, false positives per seizure, and false negatives per seizure; true negatives were approximated by 1-second epochs containing no manually or automatically detected seizure. This LFP-based event quantification is related to the proposed method because both aim to count and characterize seizure events in larval zebrafish, including PTZ-induced and genetic seizure models, but the paper does not use whole-brain calcium fluctuations, a 100% deltaF/F0 threshold, or area-under-the-curve amplitude measures.
[results]
Manual analysis of training data showed that PTZ-treated larvae had 580 total seizures, 38.7 +/- 34.5 per subject, with an average seizure duration of 874 ms and a cumulative duration of 613.9 s, or 40.9 +/- 39.5 s per subject. VHC-treated larvae had 13 total seizures, 0.9 +/- 2.1 per subject, average duration 287 ms, and cumulative duration 4.5 s, or 0.3 +/- 0.8 s per subject. In the genetic model, 1051 events were manually marked: 519 seizures (16.7 +/- 10.9 per subject), 385 artifacts (12.4 +/- 7.9), and 147 dubious events (4.7 +/- 4.2); average seizure duration was 101.4 ms and cumulative seizure duration was 52.7 s, or 1757.4 +/- 1104.3 ms per subject. The automated classifier was selected by cross-validated positive predictive value, but the provided excerpt does not report final test sensitivity, specificity, positive predictive value, accuracy, false positives per seizure, or false negatives per seizure. Batch automated analysis took 319 s for 30 chemical-model recordings and 424 s for 40 genetic-model recordings.
[context]
